  "notes": [
    "Browser KeyboardEvent.code identifiers name physical keys. The Fn entry is a studio placement identifier: FN_WIN is a firmware layer switch and normally produces no browser keyboard event.",
    "The encoder push maps to the consumer mute usage, represented by AudioVolumeMute. Browser delivery depends on the OS; keep this control separate from normal keycap placement targets.",
    "Windows base layer has Home, PageUp, PageDown and Delete. End is available through Fn+Home; there is no base End keycap.",
    "Mac mode changes the top-row functions and bottom modifiers. This asset deliberately represents the default Windows base layer.",
    "Coordinates specify switch/control positions. The bounding rectangle is a layout extent, not a measured enclosure outline.",
    "The encoder grid width is 1u because QMK omits w. Actual knob diameter is a separate manufacturer specification, 16 mm."
  ],
